      "question": "What is Soak (Endurance) Testing and why is it critical?",
      "answers": [
        "Running a sustained, realistic load over an extended period (12-72 hours) to detect memory leaks, resource exhaustion, and degradation.",
        "Soak testing uncovers slow memory leaks, database connection pool exhaustion, and file descriptor leaks that brief tests miss."
      ],
      "difficulty": "Intermediate"
