      "question": "What is the difference between `Promise.all()` and `Promise.allSettled()`?",
      "answers": [
        "`Promise.all()` rejects immediately if any single promise rejects (fail-fast), while `Promise.allSettled()` waits for all promises to resolve or reject and returns status objects.",
        "`Promise.all` fails fast on the first error; `Promise.allSettled` guarantees insight into the individual outcomes of every promise."
      ],
      "difficulty": "Intermediate"
